  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposal, by reason of its poor design, inappropriate massing, layout, and positioning, would fail to respond to the context and constraints of the site and surrounding area. Therefore the development would result in harm to the character and appearance of the site and surrounding area contrary to London Plan policies D3, D4, D6 and Local Plan policies CC1, CC2, and SC4.",
    "Reason : 2 - The application has failed to demonstrate that the maximum reasonable affordable housing has been proposed for the scheme. The application would therefore fail to meet the housing needs of the borough and wider London area, and would conflict with London Plan policy H4 and Local Plan policies SC2 and SC3. ",
    "Reason : 3 - The proposed development would have an unacceptable impact on the residential amenities of Rapur Court by way of loss of outlook and a harmful sense of enclosure. The application has also failed to demonstrate that the proposal would not result in loss of light to neighbouring properties. The proposal would therefore conflict with London Plan policy D6 and Local Plan policies CC2 and SC4. ",
    "Reason : 4 - The proposed development would deliver a substandard quality of accommodation, particularly in respect of quality of outlook and the quality and quantity of amenity space. Insufficient information has been submitted to demonstrate that residents would not be adversely impacted by odour, noise and air pollution. The proposal would therefore fail to comply with London Plan policies D3, D4, D6, D13, and D14 and Local Plan policies CC2, CC3, SC4, SC5, EQ4 and EQ5. ",
    "Reason : 5 - In the absence of fully completed, agreed and signed legal agreement to secure affordable housing, Travel Plan, restriction on parking permits, disabled parking bay, Carbon Offset Fund contribution, construction training, considerate contractor, contribution to improvements to Inwood park, and biodiversity gain plan, the application fails to comply with Local Plan policy IMP3. "
  ],
